 considers it a fantastic, mind-blowing talk that shows how a single skilled artist can build detailed VFX scenes quickly.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"3d world building\",\"categories\":[\"Animation & visual effects\",\"Computer graphics & rendering\"],\"tags\":[\"blender\",\"ian hubert\",\"photogrammetry\",\"camera projection\",\"vfx\"],\"quote\":null,\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":6.0},{\"vid\":\"x2H60ritjag\",\"title\":\"The Roots of Your Profits - Dr Elaine Ingham, Soil Microbiologist, Founder of Soil Foodweb Inc\",\"channel\":\"Oxford Real Farming Conference\",\"summary\":\"Soil microbiologist Elaine Ingham speaks at the Oxford Real Farming Conference on how soil organisms cycle nutrients, unlock minerals from rock and air, and why pesticides and fertilizers harm soil life. Slides are linked in the description.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite her as the explanation for why soil biology, not added fertilizer, drives plant nutrition and farm results.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"soil microbiology\",\"categories\":[\"Environment, agriculture & food systems\",\"Biology & biotechnology\"],\"tags\":[\"soil biology\",\"regenerative farming\",\"elaine ingham\",\"nutrient cycling\",\"pesticides\"],\"quote\":\"Dr Elaine Ingham delivers a salient presentation.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":6.0},{\"vid\":\"xtpgkX588nM\",\"title\":\"Milton Friedman - The Negative Income Tax\",\"channel\":\"LibertyPen\",\"summary\":\"A 1968 Firing Line interview in which Milton Friedman explains the negative income tax, a proposal to replace welfare bureaucracy with direct payments.\",\"why_hn\":\"The go-to primary source in basic income threads for Friedman's negative income tax idea.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"negative income tax\",\"categories\":[\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\",\"Labor, work & inequality\"],\"tags\":[\"milton friedman\",\"basic income\",\"welfare\",\"firing line\",\"economics\"],\"quote\":\"here's a nice intro\",\"recommenders\":7,\"score\":6.0},{\"vid\":\"ydqReeTV_vk\",\"title\":\"Evo-Devo (Despacito Biology Parody) | A Capella Science\",\"channel\":\"acapellascience\",\"summary\":\"A Capella Science parody of Despacito that sings through evolutionary developmental biology, explaining how a single cell becomes a body, including body-axis genes and dormant snake leg DNA. It runs about four minutes.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an entertaining four-minute introduction to evo-devo that works even for people who dislike the original song.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"evolutionary developmental biology\",\"categories\":[\"Evolution & genetics\",\"Satire & parody\",\"Biology & biotechnology\"],\"tags\":[\"evo-devo\",\"a capella science\",\"hox genes\",\"parody\",\"development genes\"],\"quote\":\"A TL;DR in four minutes by A Capella Science\",\"recommenders\":6,\"score\":6.0},{\"vid\":\"-4Yp3j_jk8Q\",\"title\":\"Leslie Lamport: Thinking Above the Code\",\"channel\":\"Microsoft Research\",\"summary\":\"Leslie Lamport argues that programmers, like architects, should write rigorous specifications before coding, especially for concurrent and distributed systems. The talk introduces the case for writing specs (the TLA+ mindset) as a way of thinking above the code.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points people to it as Lamport's own case for thinking and writing a spec before coding, and as an entry point to TLA+.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"formal specification\",\"categories\":[\"Logic & formal methods\",\"Distributed systems\",\"Software architecture & design\"],\"tags\":[\"tla+\",\"specification\",\"leslie lamport\",\"distributed systems\",\"software design\"],\"quote\":\"He's just saying that you should think before you code and that most specifications should be just a few sentences stating what you intend to do.\",\"