",\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\"],\"tags\":[\"c++\",\"d language\",\"language complexity\",\"scott meyers\",\"dconf\"],\"quote\":\"everyone should watch Scott Meyers's awesome presentation at a D conference\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":5.5},{\"vid\":\"KTzGBJPuJwM\",\"title\":\"But why would light \\\"slow down\\\"? | Visualizing Feynman's lecture on the refractive index\",\"channel\":\"3Blue1Brown\",\"summary\":\"3Blue1Brown visualizes Feynman's lecture on the refractive index, explaining why light appears to slow down in glass and why the effect depends on color. It builds the idea from waves produced by oscillating charges in the material.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN considers it among the clearest accessible explanations of what refractive index actually is and how light moves through transparent matter.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"optics and refraction\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"refractive index\",\"3blue1brown\",\"feynman\",\"light\",\"physics\",\"waves\"],\"quote\":\"probably the clearest reasonably accessible explanation of this topic anywhere to date\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":5.5},{\"vid\":\"LKnqECcg6Gw\",\"title\":\"Computer Color is Broken\",\"channel\":\"minutephysics\",\"summary\":\"MinutePhysics explains that computers store brightness nonlinearly, so blurring and blending colors in raw RGB gives wrong, dark results. It shows why mixed colors, such as in gradients, look off.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as the accessible go-to explanation of gamma and color blending errors in image programs.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"gamma and color blending\",\"categories\":[\"Computer graphics & rendering\",\"Graphic design & typography\"],\"tags\":[\"gamma correction\",\"srgb\",\"color blending\",\"gradients\",\"image processing\"],\"quote\":\"I found minutephysics' treatment of this subject to be really pleasant and easy to grok.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":5.5},{\"vid\":\"MijmeoH9LT4\",\"title\":\"Characters, Symbols and the Unicode Miracle - Computerphile\",\"channel\":\"Computerphile\",\"summary\":\"Tom Scott explains for Computerphile how Unicode and UTF-8 grew out of messy older character encodings to become the web's standard. It covers why the design works and how it handles worldwide text.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN treats it as the go-to short explanation of UTF-8, praised for making the topic stick.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"unicode and utf-8\",\"categories\":[\"Graphic design & typography\",\"Information theory & signal processing\",\"Networking & internet infrastructure\"],\"tags\":[\"unicode\",\"utf-8\",\"character encoding\",\"computerphile\",\"tom scott\"],\"quote\":\"a wonderful, terse, very informative video describing how utf-8 encoding works and why\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":5.5},{\"vid\":\"NHopJHSlVo4\",\"title\":\"Keep your goals to yourself | Derek Sivers\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"A four-minute TED talk in which Derek Sivers argues that announcing your goals can make you less likely to achieve them. He cites psychology research going back to the 1920s.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters credit it with changing how they handle plans and recommend it as a short, sourced talk.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"goal setting psychology\",\"categories\":[\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"Psychology & human behavior\"],\"tags\":[\"motivation\",\"goals\",\"productivity\",\"psychology\",\"ted\"],\"quote\":\"I did not really put two and two together until I saw this talk[0] many years ago and it clicked.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":5.5},{\"vid\":\"NRoUC9P1PmA\",\"title\":\"ZFS: The Last Word in File Systems Part 1\",\"channel\":\"Deirdré Straughan\",\"summary\":\"Jeff Bonwick and Bill Moore, the creators of ZFS, present 'ZFS: The Last Word in File Systems' at t