    ",{\"vid\":\"I7IdS-PbEgI\",\"title\":\"React.js Conf 2015 - Immutable Data and React\",\"channel\":\"Meta Developers\",\"summary\":\"Lee Byron of Facebook explains how persistent immutable data structures work and how to use them in React apps with Immutable.js. He covers memoization benefits and avoiding coupling through shared mutable state.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a clear explanation of immutable data structures such as tries, and of the case for immutability with React and Flux.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"immutable data in react\",\"categories\":[\"Web development\",\"Functional programming\",\"Algorithms & data structures\"],\"tags\":[\"immutable.js\",\"react\",\"persistent data structures\",\"tries\",\"flux\"],\"quote\":\"there's a great conference talk on this topic by Lee Byron from Facebook\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"If61baWF4GE\",\"title\":\"Why Russia is Invading Ukraine\",\"channel\":\"RealLifeLore\",\"summary\":\"RealLifeLore explains with maps why Russia invaded Ukraine, focusing on energy resources, security buffers, Black Sea access and Crimea's strategic value.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN users shared it during the early 2022 invasion as a clear, map-driven overview of Russia's economic and strategic motives.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"russia ukraine war motives\",\"categories\":[\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\"],\"tags\":[\"russia\",\"ukraine\",\"geopolitics\",\"oil and gas\",\"crimea\"],\"quote\":\"is an excellent overview of the history that lead to this moment\",\"recommenders\":10,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"IroPQ150F6c\",\"title\":\"Andrew Kelley: A Practical Guide to Applying Data Oriented Design (DoD)\",\"channel\":\"ChimiChanga\",\"summary\":\"Andrew Kelley, creator of Zig, presents practical data-oriented design techniques for shrinking memory footprint and making programs cache friendly. He ends with a case study of how these ideas sped up the Zig compiler.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as one of the best talks on data-oriented design, applying struct-of-arrays and compact data layouts to a real compiler.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"data-oriented design\",\"categories\":[\"Software performance & optimization\",\"Software architecture & design\",\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\"],\"tags\":[\"zig\",\"andrew kelley\",\"cache efficiency\",\"struct of arrays\",\"compilers\",\"performance\"],\"quote\":\"A good introduction to SoA (for anyone curious) are the two most famous Data-Oriented Design talks\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"JHGkaShoyNs\",\"title\":\"Greg Young - CQRS and Event Sourcing - Code on the Beach 2014\",\"channel\":\"Code on the Beach\",\"summary\":\"Greg Young's Code on the Beach 2014 talk on CQRS and event sourcing. He argues mature domains are built on facts that occurred rather than current state, and covers the business and technical benefits.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN developers recommend it as the talk that changed how they model systems, and as a clear intro to event sourcing's motivations.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"event sourcing\",\"categories\":[\"Software architecture & design\",\"Databases & storage\"],\"tags\":[\"cqrs\",\"event sourcing\",\"greg young\",\"domain modeling\",\"software architecture\"],\"quote\":\"forever changed how I think about modeling systems, preserving history\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"Jib2AmRb_rk\",\"title\":\"SQLite: The Database at the Edge of the Network with Dr. Richard Hipp\",\"channel\":\"Method\",\"summary\":\"SQLite creator Richard Hipp gives a history of SQLite and explains where it shines as a database at the edge of the network with no DBA. He covers long-term support, testing and how it is used in products.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an enthusiastic, funny talk straight from the creator, and cites it for facts like the name's pronunciation and Airbus support.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"sqlite\",\"categories\":[\"Databases & storage\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"sqlite\",\"richard hipp\",\"embedded databases\",\"testing\",\"long-term support\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend to watch it, if only to get a sense of the smart and funny energy that Dr Richard Hipp puts off!\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"Jzfpyo-q-RM\",\"title\":\"Worst Nuclear Accidents in History\",\"channel\":\"Kurzgesagt – In a Nutshell\",\"summary\":\"Kurzgesagt compares how many people nuclear accidents have killed against other energy sources. It walks through the worst nuclear accidents and puts their death tolls in context per unit of energy.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as a short, well-sourced overview showing that fossil fuels kill far more people than nuclear power.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"nuclear safety\",\"categories\":[\"Nuclear power & fusion\",\"Animals & nature\"],\"tags\":[\"nuclear accidents\",\"energy deaths\",\"chernobyl\",\"fossil fuels\",\"kurzgesagt\"],\"quote\":\"I really recommend watching this short video which gives a really excellent overview\",\"recommenders\":7,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"Ki_Af_o9Q9s\",\"title\":\"7 Minutes of Terror: The Challenges of Getting to Mars\",\"channel\":\"NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory\",\"summary\":\"NASA JPL engineers explain the final minutes of the Curiosity rover's entry, descent and landing on Mars, which combined aerobraking, a parachute and a skycrane. It lays out the tight sequence of events that all had to work automatically.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN repeatedly recommends it as an awe-inspiring example of engineering problem solving and the go-to explainer on how Mars landings work.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"mars landing engineering\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Robotics\"],\"tags\":[\"curiosity rover\",\"skycrane\",\"entry descent landing\",\"nasa jpl\",\"space engineering\"],\"quote\":\"If you have not watched the seven minutes of terror video produced by NASA, you absolutely must.\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"L5pUA3LsEaw\",\"title\":\"Why Not Just: Think of AGI Like a Corporation?\",\"channel\":\"Robert Miles AI Safety \",\"summary\":\"Robert Miles asks whether corporations can be thought of as artificial general superintelligences and how far the analogy holds. He argues the differences, such as being limited by employees' capabilities, matter for AI safety.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as an accessible rebuttal to the claim that AI risk is just corporate risk.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ai safety\",\"categories\":[\"AI safety, AGI & impact\"],\"tags\":[\"agi\",\"corporations\",\"ai risk\",\"superintelligence\",\"robert miles\"],\"quote\":\"He presents the material in a very interesting and accessible way.\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"LEZv-kQUSi4\",\"title\":\"Stuart Halloway - Narcissistic Design\",\"channel\":\"Reaktor\",\"summary\":\"Stuart Halloway's satirical talk describes how to protect yourself from industry change by spreading complexity through systems while following idiomatic practice. It uses this inversion to catalog software design anti-patterns.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters love it as a witty and insightful tour of design anti-patterns, applicable to DSLs, OOP and API design.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"software design anti-patterns\",\"categories\":[\"Software architecture & design\",\"Functional programming\",\"Satire & parody\"],\"tags\":[\"software design\",\"complexity\",\"anti-patterns\",\"clojure\",\"maintainability\"],\"quote\":\"a great talk by Stuart Halloway called Narcissistic Design.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"LQmTKxI4Wn4\",\"title\":\"Electron transport chain\",\"channel\":\"Harvard Online\",\"summary\":\"A short Harvard Online animated lesson on how the mitochondrial electron transport chain works. It shows proton pumping and the machinery that drives ATP synthesis.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters share it to show how cells work as nanoscale machines, which many find mind-blowing.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"cell biology\",\"categories\":[\"Biology & biotechnology\"],\"tags\":[\"mitochondria\",\"electron transport chain\",\"atp synthase\",\"proton gradient\",\"biochemistry\"],\"quote\":\"To get a flavour of the nanomachine aspect of it all, check out this video on electron transport across membranes\",\"recommenders\":6,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"LRhbcDzbGSU\",\"title\":\"GET LAMP: The Text Adventure Documentary\",\"channel\":\"Google TechTalks\",\"summary\":\"Jason Scott discusses making his documentary GET LAMP at a Google Tech Talk and screens part of the film. It covers the history of text adventures and interactive fiction, with interviews of Infocom developers and others.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it to anyone interested in text adventures, Infocom, MUDs and early computer gaming history.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"text adventure history\",\"categories\":[\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"History of computing\"],\"tags\":[\"get lamp\",\"jason scott\",\"infocom\",\"interactive fiction\",\"zork\",\"retro games\"],\"quote\":\"Recommend watching “Get lamp” documentary to fans of MUDs, text adventures\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"LbH1ZDImaI8\",\"title\":\"Is SpaceX's Raptor engine the king of rocket engines?\",\"channel\":\"Everyday Astronaut\",\"summary\":\"Everyday Astronaut explains the basic physics of rocket engines, the main engine cycles and fuel types, then compares SpaceX's methane-fueled full-flow staged combustion Raptor to other engines. It runs 