ity, wasted package management effort and how Windows does app distribution better.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited constantly in Flatpak, packaging and ABI-compatibility debates as Linus's blunt, insightful take on shipping software for Linux.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"linux desktop packaging\",\"categories\":[\"Linux & open-source ecosystems\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"linus torvalds\",\"application distribution\",\"backwards compatibility\",\"flatpak\",\"distros\"],\"quote\":\"Linus Torvalds explains it perfectly\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"Q3uvzcY2Xug\",\"title\":\"The End of Suburbia - 52 minute documentary on peak oil\",\"channel\":\"endofsuburbia\",\"summary\":\"A 52-minute short version of the documentary The End of Suburbia, about peak oil and the end of cheap energy. It argues that American suburbs depend on cheap oil and may become the slums of the future.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in threads on suburbs, energy and urbanism as an entertaining, if biased, case for suburbia's dependence on cheap oil.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"peak oil and suburbia\",\"categories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\",\"Earth & energy (other)\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"peak oil\",\"suburbs\",\"urban planning\",\"fossil fuels\",\"kunstler\"],\"quote\":\"It's entertaining and, IMO, well worth watching even if you disagree with some of the people they interview\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"QT0I-sdoSXU\",\"title\":\"The Voting System That Gives You Two Votes\",\"channel\":\"CGP Grey\",\"summary\":\"CGP Grey explains Mixed-Member Proportional representation, the system used in New Zealand where voters get two votes. It covers how it differs from first-past-the-post.\",\"why_hn\":\"It is the go-to short explainer HN links when voting system alternatives, MMP or German-style elections come up.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"voting systems\",\"categories\":[\"US politics & elections\",\"Politics & history (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"mixed-member proportional\",\"electoral reform\",\"new zealand\",\"cgp grey\",\"elections\"],\"quote\":\"CGP Grey has a great video on it\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"QZy4Yml3LTY\",\"title\":\"John Wiegley: Putting Lenses to Work\",\"channel\":\"Bay Area Haskell\",\"summary\":\"John Wiegley's BayHac 2017 talk walks through Haskell lenses by example, showing many practical uses beyond simple record access. It is aimed at people who want to become productive with the lens library.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as the fastest way to learn lenses by example, with far-out examples later on.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"haskell lenses\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\"],\"tags\":[\"haskell\",\"lens\",\"functional programming\",\"bayhac\"],\"quote\":\"you can learn enough lens to be productive in 1 hours with this talk without reading docs at all\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"RrHnLXMTOWM\",\"title\":\"Introduction: The Chemical History of a Candle by Michael Faraday (1/6)\",\"channel\":\"engineerguy\",\"summary\":\"Bill Hammack of engineerguy introduces his series on Michael Faraday's lectures on The Chemical History of a Candle. He describes the free companion book and the commentary and caption features that help modern viewers.\",\"why_hn\":\"Praised as a masterpiece of science education that recreates Faraday's demonstrations.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"faraday candle lectures\",\"categories\":[\"Chemistry\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\",\"Scientific method & science communication\"],\"tags\":[\"michael faraday\",\"chemistry\",\"science demonstrations\",\"bill hammack\",\"science education\"],\"quote\":\"is a masterpiece in science education.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\"