plains heat as the jiggling of atoms and how we perceive it as hot and cold.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a short, joyful example of Feynman's accessible way of explaining physics, which a transcript cannot capture.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"physics explanations\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\",\"Scientific method & science communication\"],\"tags\":[\"feynman\",\"atoms\",\"heat\",\"bbc\",\"fun to imagine\"],\"quote\":\"I really recommend them. You just can't capture his joy and passion with a transcript.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"v3y8AIEX_dU\",\"title\":\"How to Move the Sun: Stellar Engines\",\"channel\":\"Kurzgesagt – In a Nutshell\",\"summary\":\"Kurzgesagt explains stellar engines such as the Shkadov thruster and Caplan thruster, which could move the Sun and solar system across the galaxy over millions of years to avoid hazards and reach new regions.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN returns to it whenever moving the solar system, Kardashev civilizations or generation ships come up, with some calling it their favorite Kurzgesagt video.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"stellar engines\",\"categories\":[\"Cosmology & astrophysics\",\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Futurism & technology and society\"],\"tags\":[\"stellar engine\",\"shkadov thruster\",\"caplan thruster\",\"kardashev scale\",\"megastructures\",\"kurzgesagt\"],\"quote\":\"Out of every video Kurzgesagt has ever produced, my favorite is this one\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"v7Mt0GYHU9A\",\"title\":\"Design Patterns vs  Anti pattern in APL by Aaron W Hsu at FnConf17\",\"channel\":\"ConfEngine\",\"summary\":\"Aaron Hsu discusses design patterns and anti-patterns in APL and why the language is productive despite its write-only reputation. He argues that idioms matter more than libraries in array languages.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a terrific talk on APL readability and