ustine sacco\",\"internet mobs\"],\"quote\":\"I'm reminded of this TED talk in these scenarios, by a journalist and author who interviewed many people who have been publicly shamed\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"wpOxbesRNBc\",\"title\":\"Dasher: information-efficient text entry\",\"channel\":\"Google TechTalks\",\"summary\":\"David MacKay's 2007 Google Tech Talk presents Dasher, a text-entry system driven by continuous gestures and a language model, reaching about 35 words per minute with one finger and 25 hands-free. It explains the information-theory reasoning behind the design.\",\"why_hn\":\"Regarded as the seminal talk on Dasher, recommended in threads on accessible and alternative text input.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"text entry interfaces\",\"categories\":[\"Information theory & signal processing\",\"UX & UI design\",\"Computer vision, speech & NLP\"],\"tags\":[\"dasher\",\"information theory\",\"language models\",\"accessibility\",\"david mackay\"],\"quote\":\"Dasher is fantastic, because it's based on rock solid information theory, designed by the late David MacKay.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"xoVJKj8lcNQ\",\"title\":\"The A.I. Dilemma - March 9, 2023\",\"channel\":\"Center for Humane Technology\",\"summary\":\"Tristan Harris and Aza Raskin of the Center for Humane Technology present why current AI capabilities pose catastrophic societal risks. They argue companies are racing to deploy without adequate safety, and that institutions must adapt. It was given before GPT-4's launch.\",\"why_hn\":\"Frequently recommended as the overview to get up to speed on AI risk, especially by people who valued The Social Dilemma.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ai risk\",\"categories\":[\"AI safety, AGI & impact\",\"LLMs & generative AI\"],\"tags\":[\"ai safety\",\"llm risks\",\"center for humane technology\",\"ai race\",\"regulation\"],\"quote\":\"Here'