ard Belfer Center lecture by Matthew Bunn explaining how nuclear bombs work, including fission and fusion weapons and which parts of bomb-making are hard. It is part 1 of 2 in the Nuclear 101 series.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an entertaining, clear explanation of nuclear weapons basics from a policy expert.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"nuclear weapons basics\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\",\"Fundamental physics\",\"University lectures & courses\"],\"tags\":[\"nuclear bombs\",\"fission\",\"proliferation\",\"matthew bunn\",\"belfer center\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend the \\\"Nuclear 101: How Nuclear Bombs Work\\\" lectures by Matthew Bunn\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"zcqZHYo7ONs\",\"title\":\"Bell's Theorem: The Quantum Venn Diagram Paradox\",\"channel\":\"minutephysics\",\"summary\":\"MinutePhysics, with 3Blue1Brown, explains Bell's theorem using a Venn diagram paradox and polarizing filters. It shows why no local hidden variable theory can reproduce quantum correlations.\",\"why_hn\":\"Repeatedly recommended as the most accessible explanation of Bell's inequality, reducing it to a simple counting problem.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"bell's theorem\",\"categories\":[\"Quantum physics\",\"Recreational & visual math\"],\"tags\":[\"bell's theorem\",\"quantum entanglement\",\"hidden variables\",\"polarization\",\"nonlocality\"],\"quote\":\"did a two part collab that simplifies some of it down to a counting problem that'd be suitable for grade school.\",\"recommenders\":8,\"score\":5.0},{\"vid\":\"-4EDhdAHrOg\",\"title\":\"It's Not About The Nail\",\"channel\":\"Jason Headley\",\"summary\":\"A two-minute comedy sketch in which a woman describes her problems while a visible nail sticks out of her head, and her partner keeps trying to fix it instead of listening. It dramatizes the gap between wanting empathy and being offered solutions.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters link it as the quickest memorable illustration of listening versus problem-solving, and as shorthand in threads on empathy and support.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"listening vs problem solving\",\"categories\":[\"Stand-up & sketch comedy\",\"Psychology & human behavior\"],\"tags\":[\"empathy\",\"communication\",\"relationships\",\"sketch\",\"emotional support\"],\"quote\":\"This was the single most impactful thing I've ever been told to watch when it comes to 'solving' vs 'listening'.\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":4.5},{\"vid\":\"-4FXLQoLDBA\",\"title\":\"Animated Voting Methods\",\"channel\":\"Unify The Vote\",\"summary\":\"An animated simulation comparing single-winner voting methods such as plurality, instant runoff and STAR. Colored regions show which candidate wins as a randomized electorate shifts across a two-dimensional political space, building on Ka-Ping Yee's earlier diagrams.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite it in voting-reform threads as a visual argument that cardinal systems (STAR, approval) beat plurality and ranked-choice voting.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"voting systems\",\"categories\":[\"Probability & game theory\",\"Data visualization & information design\",\"US politics & elections\"],\"tags\":[\"star voting\",\"ranked-choice voting\",\"approval voting\",\"election simulation\",\"voter satisfaction\"],\"quote\":\"I always recommend this pair of videos when discussing STAR voting vs other alternative systems.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.5},{\"vid\":\"-R-eqJDQ2nU\",\"title\":\"Dr. Satchin Panda on Time-Restricted Feeding and Its Effects on Obesity, Muscle Mass & Heart Health\",\"channel\":\"FoundMyFitness\",\"summary\":\"Rhonda Patrick interviews Salk Institute researcher Satchidananda Panda about circadian rhythms and the timing of food. They cover time-restricted feeding and its links to obesity, muscle mass, heart health, and light exposure.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in threads on fasting and nutrition as a deep dive from the lead researcher on time-restricted eating.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"time-restricted feeding\",\"categories\":[\"Nutrition & diet science\",\"Fitness, sleep & longevity\"],\"tags\":[\"circadian rhythm\",\"intermittent fasting\",\"obesity\",\"sleep\",\"salk institute\"],\"quote\":\"Dr. Panda goes into detail about fasting and coffee. Great podcast about fasting.\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":4.5},{\"vid\":\"-ZxPhDC-r3w\",\"title\":\"Intrinsic Gravity by Still\",\"channel\":\"TiXL\",\"summary\":\"Intrinsic Gravity is a real-time demoscene production by Still, made with the Tooll tool for Under Construction 2014. It is a black-and-white op-art animation with a soundtrack by hoffman.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people hold it up as a standout modern demo, praising its scene transitions and how it looks on 3D displays.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"demoscene\",\"categories\":[\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\",\"Creative coding & generative art\"],\"tags\":[\"demoscene\",\"real-time graphics\",\"op art\",\"motion graphics\",\"shaders\"],\"quote\":\"It's lots of different scenes that transition beautifully from one to another\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.5},{\"vid\":\"-whuXHSL1Pg\",\"title\":\"Exposing Tether - Bitcoin's Biggest Secret\",\"channel\":\"Coffeezilla\",\"summary\":\"Coffeezilla gives a comprehensive history of Tether, the stablecoin issued by a company controlled by the owners of Bitfinex. He lays out accusations that it is not fully backed.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as the best single, entertaining overview of Tether's dubious history, and cite it when arguing Tether lacks real USD backing.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"tether and stablecoin fraud\",\"categories\":[\"Cryptography\",\"Investing & personal 