illionaire net worth by share price is misleading.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"billionaire wealth\",\"categories\":[\"Labor, work & inequality\",\"Investing & personal finance\"],\"tags\":[\"net worth\",\"stock wealth\",\"economics\",\"diversification\",\"oligarchs\"],\"quote\":\"fyi youtube video of why these simplistic comparisons of \\\"net worth\\\" based on shares-times-stockprice is meaningless\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"0UjpmT5noto\",\"title\":\"Municipal Violations: Last Week Tonight with John Oliver (HBO)\",\"channel\":\"LastWeekTonight\",\"summary\":\"John Oliver's Last Week Tonight segment on municipal violations. It shows how small fines and fees escalate for people who cannot pay and how private probation and ticket revenue can ruin lives.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as a clear account of how minor infractions punish the poor.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"municipal fines and poverty\",\"categories\":[\"Law, policing & justice\",\"Labor, work & inequality\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\"],\"tags\":[\"john oliver\",\"debtors prison\",\"private probation\",\"ferguson\",\"court fees\"],\"quote\":\"Even more relevant is his piece on municipal violations and how they can unfairly steamroll the poor with escalating fees.\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"0VyH1laOd2M\",\"title\":\"Breakthrough with Healing Chronic Pain | Howard Schubiner | Talks at Google\",\"channel\":\"Talks at Google\",\"summary\":\"Dr. Howard Schubiner presents his research that much chronic pain comes from learned neural pathways rather than structural damage, and outlines a treatment approach based on that view.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended to people with chronic pain, fatigue or RSI as a rigorous but balanced case that pain does not always mean injury.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"chronic pain neuroscience\",\"categories\":[\"Neuroscience & the brain\",\"Medicine & infectious disease\",\"Mental health & neurodiversity\"],\"tags\":[\"chronic pain\",\"mind-body\",\"psychosomatic\",\"rsi\",\"howard schubiner\"],\"quote\":\"The author links to Schubiner's talk on chronic pain, which I heartily recommend as the right balance of rigor and tone\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"0g9BcZvQbXU\",\"title\":\"Consistent Technical Documents Using Emacs and Org Mode\",\"channel\":\"spudlyo\",\"summary\":\"A demo of writing technical documents in Emacs Org mode using org-babel, so that code blocks and generated content stay consistent when things change. The author shares the demo files and his dotfiles.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as a practical illustration of what Org mode and literate programming can do for documentation.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"emacs org mode documentation\",\"categories\":[\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\",\"Software practice, open source & careers\"],\"tags\":[\"emacs\",\"org mode\",\"org babel\",\"literate programming\",\"technical writing\"],\"quote\":\"I think does a pretty good job of illustrating the power of Org.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"1H3xQaf7BFI\",\"title\":\"THE NVIDIA AI GPU BLACK MARKET | Investigating Smuggling, Corruption, & Governments\",\"channel\":\"Gamers Nexus\",\"summary\":\"A Gamers Nexus investigative documentary on the black market for Nvidia AI GPUs, following smugglers, middlemen, and buyers, including reporting from China. It examines how export-restricted chips reach their users.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as real on-the-ground reporting on how banned GPUs get into China despite export controls.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"nvidia gpu smuggling\",\"categories\":[\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\",\"Computer architecture & CPUs\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\"],\"tags\":[\"nvidia\",\"export controls\",\"gpu smuggling\",\"china\",\"investigative journalism\"],\"quote\":\"Gamers Nexus has a good video where his team travelled to China and did some actual investigative journalism\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"1Y1ya-yF35g\",\"title\":\"Nuclear Weapons: Last Week Tonight with John Oliver (HBO)\",\"channel\":\"LastWeekTonight\",\"summary\":\"A Last Week Tonight segment on the US nuclear arsenal and how poorly it is maintained and secured. It covers weapons accidents, outdated launch protocols and security problems.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a funny but sobering overview of nuclear weapons safety failures.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"nuclear weapons safety\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\"],\"tags\":[\"nuclear weapons\",\"john oliver\",\"arsenal safety\",\"weapons accidents\",\"disarmament\"],\"quote\":\"John Olivers episode on it is also amazing.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"1rZ-JorHJEY\",\"title\":\"Hacking with Andrew and Brad: tip.golang.org\",\"channel\":\"The Go Programming Language\",\"summary\":\"A roughly hour-long live hacking session in which Go team members Andrew Gerrand and Brad Fitzpatrick write the new version of tip.golang.org, the site serving leading-edge Go documentation. It is unedited pair programming on a real Go project.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people point to it as a rare chance to watch skilled developers write real code live, pair programming and explaining as they go.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"live coding in go\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Software practice, open source & careers\"],\"tags\":[\"golang\",\"pair programming\",\"live coding\",\"web services\",\"brad fitzpatrick\"],\"quote\":\"It's just something to watch the pros doing live coding.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"1wAaI_6b9JE\",\"title\":\"Four Dimensional Maths: Things to See and Hear in the Fourth Dimension - with Matt Parker\",\"channel\":\"The Royal Institution\",\"summary\":\"Matt Parker gives a hands-on Royal Institution talk on how four-dimensional shapes appear in a 3D world, with props like straw frames, Mobius strips and a knitted hat. It is a playful general-audience tour of the fourth dimension.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an enjoyable, accessible talk for building intuition about higher dimensions.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"four-dimensional geometry\",\"categories\":[\"Recreational & visual math\",\"Pure mathematics\"],\"tags\":[\"matt parker\",\"4d cube\",\"topology\",\"mobius strip\",\"recreational math\"],\"quote\":\"I love Matt Parker's take on the fourth dimension\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"24R8JObNNQ4\",\"title\":\"From the DMZ Into the Hermit Kingdom - Inside North Korea (Part 1/3)\",\"channel\":\"VICE\",\"summary\":\"Vice founder Shane Smith travels to North Korea, speaking with refugees in South Korea before crossing the DMZ. It is part one of a three-part documentary with rare on-the-ground footage.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as a rare, eye-opening look inside North Korea, though one notes such tours are staged.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"north korea\",\"categories\":[\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\"],\"tags\":[\"vice\",\"shane smith\",\"dmz\",\"north korea\",\"travel documentary\",\"kim jong il\"],\"quote\":\"Vice has a three-part 1-hour-total documentary on North Korea with footage from the country.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"2IT2oAzTcvU\",\"title\":\"Nina Kollars - Confessions of an Nespresso Money Mule - DEF CON 27 Conference\",\"channel\":\"DEFCONConference\",\"summary\":\"At DEF CON 27, Nina Kollars tells how buying Nespresso capsules on eBay led her to investigate fraudsters