\"Security & hacking\"],\"tags\":[\"chris domas\",\"defcon\",\"obfuscation\",\"anti-reverse-engineering\",\"assembly\"],\"quote\":\"Christopher Domas is one of my absolute favorite all-time hackers. He does such a fantastic job of explaining his work.\",\"recommenders\":4,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"Hzb37RyagCQ\",\"title\":\"36C3 -  Open Source is Insufficient to Solve Trust Problems in Hardware\",\"channel\":\"media.ccc.de\",\"summary\":\"A 36C3 talk by Bunnie Huang arguing that open source is necessary but not sufficient for trustworthy hardware, because verifying hardware is destructive and so creates a time-of-check/time-of-use gap. It surveys supply chain security and classes of hardware attacks, and presents the Betrusted approach to narrowing that gap.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it whenever the question is how far hardware can be trusted, including FPGAs, supply chain attacks and firmware TPMs.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"hardware trust and supply chain security\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"Semiconductors & chip manufacturing\",\"Hacker culture & free software\"],\"tags\":[\"hardware security\",\"supply chain\",\"fpga\",\"open hardware\",\"betrusted\",\"toctou\"],\"quote\":\"Here's an excellent talk that addresses your question\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":4.0},{\"vid\":\"IRVdiHu1VCc\",\"title\":\"Learning from dirty jobs | Mike Rowe\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"Mike Rowe, host of Dirty Jobs, shares stories from messy real-world jobs in this TED talk. He argues that hard work has been unjustly degraded in society.\",\"why_hn\":\"It comes up in threads on career choice, trades, handiness and the 'follow your passion' advice.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"value of hard work\",\"categories\":[\"Labor, work & inequality\",\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"Ideas & learning (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"mike rowe\",\"dirty jobs\",\"careers\",\"trades\